#
# A logic:ContextAssembly that records what was surfaced and what was withheld, states
# why it was withheld, and never says WHOSE run it served. Unbound, the record answers
# the audit question about nobody: the guidance versions it names were surfaced to some
# occurrence, and no later reader can say which — so "the operator saw the objection and
# proceeded" is unrecoverable for every run at once.
# MUST trip logic:ContextAssemblyNamesItsEnactmentConstraint, and it alone. The two
# exclusion laws are guarded here and PASS on their merits rather than vacuously: the
# withheld item carries its logic:assemblyExclusionReason, and the included and excluded
# items are different items. The assembly also records the guidance revision it was
# judged under, so gmeow:GuidanceVersionRecordedConstraint — the work-orchestration law
# that governs this same kernel class — is satisfied too, and the one unanswerable
# question left is WHOSE run this record is about.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

ex:assemblyServingNobody a logic:ContextAssembly ;
    logic:assemblyGuidanceVersion ex:adrReviewGuidanceV7 ;
    logic:assemblyIncluded ex:adrRiskNote ;
    logic:assemblyExcluded ex:staleSecurityObjection ;
    logic:assemblyExclusionReason "Superseded by revision 4 of the threat model." ;
    rdfs:label "a context assembly that served no nameable run"@en .
